              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Darinnia Bynam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been saerching for garlic crabs for the longest time. my sister told me to try all recipes and i'm glad i did. It was an easy and tasty process. 2 thumbs up lol"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tina Foley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My favorite recipe ever! Split the shells before you throw the crab legs in. Once done remove the legs and pour the butter sauce into a dish for dipping....mmmmm good.",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-17T08:05:44.947Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If your lucky - your grocer will have precut crab which isn’t nearly as dangerous as trying to cut your own. I admit, I am not that skilled with a knife and a hard shell like crab is daunting so I only did a few and then decided to skip and take my chances and use my crab-cracker and fork. Preparation aside, this recipe is AMAZING! Like scampi for your crab. I used KerryGold butter and added a splash of buttery Chardonnay just before adding the crab. This is absolutely divine! We spooned the butter garlic sauce over each plate of crab and as we pulled that succulent, sweet meat out - dipped again in either what butter was on our plates or into the pan itself. Cook time is spot on. Oui! Died and went to heaven in this one! Thanks Tamaralynn!",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-13T01:35:48.502Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carrie Smith-Hardee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy and delicious! I’ve never cooked crab legs in a skillet before. It totally worked. Added lemon pepper and a squeeze of fresh lemon. Also poured the extra garlic butter in the pan over white sticky rice with a little added olive oil and lemon pepper. We were devouring this whole meal!",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-08T04:43:40.327Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angela HJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family loves this recipe, however, my husband does not trust that they will cook completely in the butter so we usually steam them for about 5 minutes before putting them in the butter sauce. We've made them several times &amp; everyone absolutely loves them. This last time I added Old Bay &amp; Cayenne based on some of the reviews &amp; they were even better!",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-21T06:31:47.837Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mensh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Overcome the messy shell issue by steaming the crab legs for a bit, removing the shell and proceeding with the recipe. Add the shells and any liquid from cooking them when you make the garlic butter sauce. Keeping the shells in the sauce, lightly saute the \"naked legs\" in the enhanced garlic butter sauce. Prepare more legs than anticipated as all gobbled up quickly. It solves the \"messy to eat\" issue and hopefully slows down the rate at which the legs are eaten.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-05T06:55:54.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "David L Oppenheim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe but i used fresh chives instead of parsley. And I think next time I would use scissors to cut it up better before cooking",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-06T02:49:33.045Z"
          },
          {
