            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nickey1016"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was amazing! I live in Florida and I am obsessed with snow crab legs. Instead of going to the 'many' crab houses around and getting their garlic butter covered crabs. I decided to make my own. This recipe was great. I boiled my crab legs in old bay seasoning with a few other spices. Also added red potatoes to the pot. I made this on the side to dip the crabs and potatoes in. I didn't measure anything. I just did it by sight and to my taste. This will definitely be my go to whenever I make crab legs.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-28T18:54:30.883Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Caryn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I baked the crab legs at 400*until warm. I served this sauce on the side. I did add Old Bay seasoning and Italian blend to it too. Very easy, very delicious. Will make it again.\n- Caryn",
            "datePublished": "2013-11-27T19:24:14.710Z"
